WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.511 --> 00:00:16.633
last the voyage was about to begin.

2
00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:22.118
"There!" exclaimed the doctor, "I think we're ready to sail!"

3
00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:25.421
Tommy rubbed his hands together with excitement.

4
00:00:25.921 --> 00:00:28.764
When he saw his crying mother, he turned his back.

5
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.283
Tommy did not want her to see how excited he was to leave.

6
00:00:33.303 --> 00:00:38.207
"Why can't we come with you, Dr.

7
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.769
Dolittle!" Gub-Gub snorted loudly.

8
00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:42.991
"It's not fair!"

9
00:00:43.491 --> 00:00:44.772
barked Jip angrily.

10
00:00:44.792 --> 00:00:48.695
"I can cook for you," quacked Dab-Dab.

11
00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:52.198
"Hmm, what time is it?"

12
00:00:52.779 --> 00:00:57.860
yawned a sleepy Too-Too.

13
00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.722
Dr. Dolittle knelt down before them.

14
00:00:59.742 --> 00:01:06.606
"I wish all of you could come," he said kindly, "but the boat is too small.

15
00:01:06.626 --> 00:01:12.730
"Besides," he continued, "who is going to take care of the house and garden?"

16
00:01:13.511 --> 00:01:15.472
The animals hung their heads low.

17
00:01:16.393 --> 00:01:19.515
They really wanted to go on this voyage with the doctor.

18
00:01:19.535 --> 00:01:22.257
"Am I late?"

19
00:01:23.057 --> 00:01:24.718
a voice shouted from a distance.

20
00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:27.020
Tommy squinted his eyes.

21
00:01:28.428 --> 00:01:30.889
"Oh!" he said, "it's the prince."

22
00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:34.390
The prince wore a white sailor suit and hat.

23
00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:37.551
He carried two very large suitcases.

24
00:01:37.571 --> 00:01:40.591
"Your Highness," Dr.

25
00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:41.592
Dolittle began.

26
00:01:42.572 --> 00:01:44.112
The prince smiled broadly.

27
00:01:44.132 --> 00:01:47.093
"On this voyage I am not a prince.

28
00:01:47.633 --> 00:01:49.614
I'm a sailor," he said.

29
00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:54.595
"You may call me ."—he paused—"Charles."

30
00:01:54.615 --> 00:01:57.804
"Okay Charles," said Dr.

31
00:01:57.824 --> 00:02:07.867
Dolittle. "Er...Charles," he continued, chuckling, "I'm afraid you can't bring both those bags."

32
00:02:07.887 --> 00:02:09.708
"Why not?"

33
00:02:10.388 --> 00:02:11.208
the prince asked.

34
00:02:11.228 --> 00:02:14.509
"We don't have enough room," Dr.

35
00:02:14.549 --> 00:02:15.489
Dolittle replied.

36
00:02:15.509 --> 00:02:24.632
"But I need all my books," said Charles, "and my rock collection, my shoes, my cooking spices, my

37
00:02:25.732 --> 00:02:29.673
But in the end, Charles had to leave everything behind.

38
00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.814
Dr. Dolittle clapped his hands.

39
00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:35.775
"Well, we should get going."

40
00:02:36.855 --> 00:02:38.275
Tommy hugged his parents.

41
00:02:39.496 --> 00:02:43.957
"Remember to brush your teeth every morning," sobbed his mother.

42
00:02:43.977 --> 00:02:48.298
"Here," his father said, "I made these for you."

43
00:02:49.038 --> 00:02:51.759
He handed Tommy a brand new pair of shoes.

44
00:02:51.779 --> 00:02:55.420
"I will wear them every day," Tommy promised.

45
00:02:57.628 --> 00:02:59.330
Dr. Dolittle looked around.

46
00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:02.673
"That's odd," he said.

47
00:03:02.693 --> 00:03:04.555
"Where did everyone go?"

48
00:03:05.155 --> 00:03:07.377
The animals were nowhere to be seen.

49
00:03:07.397 --> 00:03:10.941
"I saw them here a minute ago," said Tommy.

50
00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:15.905
"They must have gone home because they were too upset," said the doctor.

51
00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:22.612
Then he cupped his hands and shouted: "All aboard on The Curlew!"

52
00:03:25.964 --> 00:03:28.885
As they left Puddleby, Tommy looked over the map.

53
00:03:28.905 --> 00:03:32.467
"I can't find Spider Monkey Island," he said.

54
00:03:32.487 --> 00:03:35.268
"Of course not," answered the doctor.

55
00:03:35.928 --> 00:03:36.909
"What do you mean?"

56
00:03:37.389 --> 00:03:38.169
asked Tommy.

57
00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:41.971
"Spider Monkey Island is a floating island!"

58
00:03:42.451 --> 00:03:43.532
replied the doctor.

59
00:03:43.552 --> 00:03:46.013
"A floating island?"

60
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:47.453
Tommy cried out.

61
00:03:47.473 --> 00:03:50.475
"Then how are we going to find it?"

62
00:03:50.495 --> 00:03:56.209
"Don't worry," said the doctor, "Miranda told us where to look."

63
00:03:56.229 --> 00:04:02.150
"And the whales and eagles will tell us how to get there," Polynesia added.

64
00:04:03.731 --> 00:04:05.051
Tommy put the map down.

65
00:04:05.071 --> 00:04:08.012
"I guess we won't need this," he said.

66
00:04:08.032 --> 00:04:11.193
"Dr. Dolittle!"

67
00:04:11.613 --> 00:04:12.913
Charles ran toward them.

68
00:04:13.674 --> 00:04:15.374
The doctor turned to look at him.

69
00:04:15.394 --> 00:04:22.076
"I was making sandwiches for our lunch," said Charles, "when I discovered something interesting."

70
00:04:22.516 --> 00:04:24.138
He motioned for them to follow.

71
00:04:27.441 --> 00:04:30.985
Charles put a finger to his lips and tiptoed into the kitchen.

72
00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:33.247
Everyone followed him quietly.

73
00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:36.510
"Now watch this," he whispered.

74
00:04:37.411 --> 00:04:40.634
Charles made a large sandwich and placed it on the table.

75
00:04:41.535 --> 00:04:45.900
The cupboard door opened and something snatched the sandwich off the table.

76
00:04:48.636 --> 00:04:52.937
Dr. Dolittle quietly went to the cupboard and swung the door open.

77
00:04:52.957 --> 00:04:55.718
"Gub-Gub!" the doctor shouted.

78
00:04:56.298 --> 00:04:57.799
The pig began to cry.

79
00:04:57.819 --> 00:04:59.699
"I'm sorry, Dr.

80
00:04:59.759 --> 00:05:02.520
Dolittle! Jip made me do it."

81
00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.321
A deep growling sound came from a sack of potatoes.

82
00:05:07.062 --> 00:05:08.762
Tommy went over and opened it.

83
00:05:08.782 --> 00:05:15.004
"Sorry, Doctor," Jip barked, from inside the bag.

84
00:05:16.092 --> 00:05:19.254
"Well, it looks as if we have a few uninvited guests!"

85
00:05:19.654 --> 00:05:20.714
the doctor remarked.

86
00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:24.736
"Uh, Doctor," Tommy pointed to a large barrel.

87
00:05:24.756 --> 00:05:28.578
"I think that barrel just coughed."

88
00:05:28.598 --> 00:05:33.340
Dr. Dolittle opened the lid and found old Matthew covered in flour.

89
00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:37.322
"Ahhh," muttered Matthew wiped his nose.
